# Page objects (`pages/**`)

One class per page or feature area. It owns locators and actions; it never owns test outcomes.

- Constructor: `this.page`, `readonly url = '/route'`, every locator as a `readonly` property with `.describe('<Name> <role>')`.
- Locator priority: `getByRole` / `getByLabel` → `[data-test=…]` / `[data-testid=…]` → `getByText`. Never CSS classes, ids or XPath.
- Verify locators on the live page with `playwright-cli` (`open`, `snapshot`, `eval "el => el.getAttribute('data-test')" <ref>`) before adding or changing them.
- Always implement `load()` (`page.goto(this.url)`) and `waitLoad()` (`test.step` + `waitFor({ state: 'visible' })` on the most stable anchor: heading or primary action, never a spinner).
- Action methods: verb + noun (`submitLoginForm`, `addItemsToCart`), take all data as parameters, return data only when the test needs it.
- Only `test` is imported from `@playwright/test` (for `test.step`). Never `expect`. Enforced by `no-restricted-imports` and `no-restricted-syntax`.
- No test data, no credentials, no `process.env` reads inside page objects.

```ts
// WRONG — assertion inside an action
async addToCart() {
  await this.addButton.click();
  await expect(this.cartBadge).toHaveText('1');
}

// CORRECT — action only; the spec asserts
async addToCart(): Promise<void> {
  await this.addButton.click();
}
```

Adding a page object is not finished until `fixtures/page.fixtures.ts` has its entry and `pnpm lint` passes.
